Do not touch the cache while simultaneous sessions are allowed

SimultaneousSessionsMiddleware._process_request in
horizon/middleware/simultaneous_sessions.py runs on every request,
because openstack_dashboard/settings.py lists the middleware for all of
them, and it runs whatever SIMULTANEOUS_SESSIONS says. It reads
user_pk_<pk>_restrict from caches['default'] and, in every case but a
disconnect mismatch, writes the session key of the request to the same
key with SESSION_TIMEOUT as expiry. Only the disconnect branch reads
the entry; with the default allow the two calls serve nothing.

The calls cost twice. They are two Memcached round trips per request:
with Memcached delayed by 100 ms, the p50 of GET /auth/login/ went from
23 ms to 921 ms and that of POST /auth/logout/, which renders no
template, from 4 ms to 304 ms (C5C3/playground#165). And with Django's
signed-cookie session store the session key is the value of the
session cookie the request sent. The cookie is signed, not encrypted,
and decodes without SECRET_KEY, so the session cookie of every
logged-in user, Keystone token included, sits in the shared Memcached
for SESSION_TIMEOUT, readable by any client of that Memcached (#1847).

The patch returns at the top of _process_request unless
SIMULTANEOUS_SESSIONS is disconnect. The guard is != 'disconnect', not
== 'allow': upstream documents the two values allow and disconnect,
and only the disconnect branch uses the entry, so no other value needs
it. disconnect behaves as before, both calls and the stored session key
included. With the template_fragments cache alias the horizon-operator
renders, the login page then makes no Memcached call. The patch adds no
setting and needs no operator configuration.

Tests: test_simultaneous_sessions and
test_disconnect_simultaneous_sessions in
horizon/test/unit/middleware/test_simultaneous_sessions.py call
_process_request directly and stay unchanged and green. The patch adds
four tests there: test_allow_leaves_the_cache_alone and
test_unknown_value_leaves_the_cache_alone assert that allow and an
undocumented value leave a mocked caches untouched,
test_disconnect_records_the_session_key asserts that disconnect still
writes the session key to user_pk_<pk>_restrict, and
test_allow_passes_the_request_on asserts that the middleware hands the
request on and returns the inner response.

Proof: test_login_page_makes_no_memcached_call in
tests/container-images/verify_horizon.sh requests the login page of the
built image with the CACHES the operator renders, against a listener
that records every Memcached command, and asserts no command; under
SIMULTANEOUS_SESSIONS = "disconnect" it asserts the get and the set of
user_pk_None_restrict.

The 2026.2 twin carries the same hunks: both files are identical in
25.7.0 and 27.0.0.

Applies to horizon 25.7.0 (2026.1).

Upstream status: not yet proposed.

diff --git a/horizon/middleware/simultaneous_sessions.py b/horizon/middleware/simultaneous_sessions.py
index 5ee217a..f2765d5 100644
--- a/horizon/middleware/simultaneous_sessions.py
+++ b/horizon/middleware/simultaneous_sessions.py
@@ -32,6 +32,8 @@ class SimultaneousSessionsMiddleware(object):
         return response
 
     def _process_request(self, request):
+        if self.simultaneous_sessions != 'disconnect':
+            return
         cache = caches['default']
         cache_key = ('user_pk_{}_restrict').format(request.user.pk)
         cache_value = cache.get(cache_key)
diff --git a/horizon/test/unit/middleware/test_simultaneous_sessions.py b/horizon/test/unit/middleware/test_simultaneous_sessions.py
index 371f54f..025ac5e 100644
--- a/horizon/test/unit/middleware/test_simultaneous_sessions.py
+++ b/horizon/test/unit/middleware/test_simultaneous_sessions.py
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ from unittest import mock
 
 from django.conf import settings
 from django.contrib.sessions.backends import signed_cookies
+from django.core.cache import caches
 from django import test as django_test
 from django.test.utils import override_settings
 
@@ -59,3 +60,43 @@ class SimultaneousSessionsMiddlewareTest(django_test.TestCase):
         self.request.session._set_session_key('987654321')
         mw._process_request(self.request)
         mock_delete.assert_called_once_with()
+
+    @override_settings(SIMULTANEOUS_SESSIONS='allow')
+    @mock.patch('horizon.middleware.simultaneous_sessions.caches')
+    def test_allow_leaves_the_cache_alone(self, mock_caches):
+        mw = middleware.SimultaneousSessionsMiddleware(
+            self.get_response)
+
+        self.request.session._set_session_key('123456789')
+        mw._process_request(self.request)
+        mock_caches.__getitem__.assert_not_called()
+
+    @override_settings(SIMULTANEOUS_SESSIONS='deny')
+    @mock.patch('horizon.middleware.simultaneous_sessions.caches')
+    def test_unknown_value_leaves_the_cache_alone(self, mock_caches):
+        mw = middleware.SimultaneousSessionsMiddleware(
+            self.get_response)
+
+        self.request.session._set_session_key('123456789')
+        mw._process_request(self.request)
+        mock_caches.__getitem__.assert_not_called()
+
+    @override_settings(SIMULTANEOUS_SESSIONS='disconnect')
+    def test_disconnect_records_the_session_key(self):
+        mw = middleware.SimultaneousSessionsMiddleware(
+            self.get_response)
+
+        self.request.user.pk = '456'
+        self.request.session._set_session_key('123456789')
+        mw._process_request(self.request)
+        self.assertEqual('123456789',
+                         caches['default'].get('user_pk_456_restrict'))
+
+    @override_settings(SIMULTANEOUS_SESSIONS='allow')
+    def test_allow_passes_the_request_on(self):
+        mw = middleware.SimultaneousSessionsMiddleware(
+            self.get_response)
+
+        response = mw(self.request)
+        self.assertIs(self.get_response.return_value, response)
+        self.get_response.assert_called_once_with(self.request)
